cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ehrlint in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "ehrlint: a leakage auditor for EHR prediction tasks"
abstract: >-
  ehrlint audits a finished EHR prediction dataset for the leakage patterns
  that make clinical models look good in a paper and fail in deployment:
  post-index features, outcome codes from the index encounter, treatment
  proxies, immortal time, subject and encounter overlap across splits,
  duplicate patients under two identifiers, and outcomes counted beyond the
  declared horizon. It reads MEDS or OMOP CDM input plus a task spec, runs ten
  checks, and emits a report in which every finding references the concrete
  rows that triggered it. Two rules are enforced in code: a finding without
  evidence is rejected, and a check that cannot run reports a skip with a
  reason rather than a pass. Cohort-extraction systems help define a task;
  ehrlint audits one that already exists.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
